    "title": "What time does Scottie Scheffler tee off today? How to watch world's No. 1 golfer at Augusta National",
    "text": "What time does Scottie Scheffler tee off today? How to watch world's No. 1 golfer at Augusta National originally appeared on The Sporting News. Add The Sporting News as a Preferred Source by clicking here.Scottie Scheffler is the world's No. 1 golfer.AdvertisementHe also hasn't golfed a whole lot heading into the 2026 Masters Tournament. The birth of a child kept Scheffler out of action a couple weeks ago, and so it's been a long layoff.He also wasn't playing at his best even before that, struggling in early rounds and barely making cuts before surging on the weekends.To have a chance at the green jacket, Scheffler will have to play a more complete 72 holes of golf. Someone at the Masters will put together four solid rounds. He can't be the guy that only plays a couple good rounds if he hopes to win.On Thursday, he'll have to wait around a while before getting going.AdvertisementScottie Scheffler tees off at 1:44 p.m. ET at Augusta.He is in the second-to-last group to start their rounds.Scheffler is playing with Robert MacIntyre and Gary Woodland.The only group to go after them is at 1:56 p.m. when Marco Penge, Si Woo Kim and Harris English get underway.How to watch Scottie Scheffler at MastersBroadcast coverage on Thursday is on Amazon Prime Video from 1 p.m. to 3 p.m., which will capture the early stages of Scheffler's round.From 3 p.m. onward, coverage will be on ESPN.More Masters news:",
